{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789219510,"nonce":"yQVMaWhdD1JwPeGXV7kuwCbydjs=","title":"a top-level typedef and a packaged class of the same name share one root symbol","message":"`typedef List\u003cT\u003e = haxe.ds.List\u003cT\u003e` (List.hx) registers a root symbol `List`.\n`class List\u003cT\u003e` in haxe/ds/List.hx then skips pre-registration (\"already\nexists in root scope\", registration.rs) and lower_class_declaration lowers the\nclass onto the typedef's symbol. Until 2026-09-12 that symbol was never\nregistered under `haxe.ds`, so `import haxe.ds.List` minted an empty\nplaceholder class beside it: no type parameters, no methods -- haxe.Template's\n`for (e in l)` over such a List emitted no loop at all.\n\nThe class lowering now registers the reused symbol under its package as a\nstopgap. The real fix is one symbol per declaration: the class gets its own,\nand the typedef's type aliases it.","files":null}]}